{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00291",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.35,
      "end_seconds": 5.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Ready for you, doctor. I'll stay in case you need anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.03,
      "end_seconds": 10.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Welcome, tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.25,
      "end_seconds": 16.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "So, um, I've been feeling cold all the time, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.07,
      "end_seconds": 22.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.02,
      "end_seconds": 33.87,
      "duration_seconds": 10.85,
      "text": "Honestly I can't say exactly when it started. It might have been last month or the month before, I really can't pin it down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.32,
      "end_seconds": 36.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Have you been putting on weight?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.13,
      "end_seconds": 39.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Yeah, that too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.53,
      "end_seconds": 41.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Have you had constipation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.07,
      "end_seconds": 45.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Yes, for about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.88,
      "end_seconds": 50.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.31,
      "end_seconds": 60.24,
      "duration_seconds": 8.93,
      "text": "Yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.4,
      "end_seconds": 64.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Have you had any swelling in the neck?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.5,
      "end_seconds": 69.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Not at all, uh, no swelling in the neck."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.47,
      "end_seconds": 74.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Any low mood, hair loss or heavy periods at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.64,
      "end_seconds": 80.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Well, no low mood, hair loss or heavy periods, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.78,
      "end_seconds": 83.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.48,
      "end_seconds": 88.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Okay, so no, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.21,
      "end_seconds": 91.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.79,
      "end_seconds": 94.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.03,
      "end_seconds": 110.06,
      "duration_seconds": 15.03,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.96,
      "end_seconds": 113.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Um, that's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.73,
      "end_seconds": 121.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.58,
      "end_seconds": 124.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "My mother has diabetes. My brother has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.06,
      "end_seconds": 129.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.53,
      "end_seconds": 140.95,
      "duration_seconds": 11.42,
      "text": "Not at the moment, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.85,
      "end_seconds": 145.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.03,
      "end_seconds": 155.06,
      "duration_seconds": 9.03,
      "text": "Well, uh, I'm on iron tablets, once a day. Tiotropium inhaler. I take it once a day for my chest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.2,
      "end_seconds": 158.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "How's everything else at home otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.99,
      "end_seconds": 165.13,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "Um, busy. Everyone's running in different directions at the moment, you know how it is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.55,
      "end_seconds": 167.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.2,
      "end_seconds": 169.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "No operations, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.66,
      "end_seconds": 174.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.39,
      "end_seconds": 189.2,
      "duration_seconds": 13.81,
      "text": "Hmm, yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.54,
      "end_seconds": 192.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.56,
      "end_seconds": 194.3,
      "duration_seconds": 0.74,
      "text": "No allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.83,
      "end_seconds": 209.51,
      "duration_seconds": 13.68,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.62,
      "end_seconds": 213.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Hmm, okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.62,
      "end_seconds": 216.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.54,
      "end_seconds": 220.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "I have low haemoglobin, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.04,
      "end_seconds": 222.77,
      "duration_seconds": 0.73,
      "text": "I see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.03,
      "end_seconds": 225.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.16,
      "text": "I've got COPD."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.41,
      "end_seconds": 229.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.8,
      "end_seconds": 230.5,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.04,
      "end_seconds": 242.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Okay, here we go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 243.67,
      "end_seconds": 255.91,
      "duration_seconds": 12.24,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. BP is 128 over 68, saturation 98 percent. BMI works out to 36.0, weight 81 kilos, temperature is 36.6 degrees, height 150 centimetres, heart rate 85."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.06,
      "end_seconds": 261.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.42,
      "end_seconds": 264.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.88,
      "end_seconds": 270.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.84,
      "end_seconds": 274.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "Hold your arm out like this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.07,
      "end_seconds": 287.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Reflexes are a bit slow to relax."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.46,
      "end_seconds": 290.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Can you lie back for me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.86,
      "end_seconds": 305.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Your pulse is slow, about fifty-six, and the thyroid isn't enlarged."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.05,
      "end_seconds": 306.75,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.41,
      "end_seconds": 323.6,
      "duration_seconds": 13.19,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Sorry, I'm just writing a few notes, bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.99,
      "end_seconds": 330.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "No problem, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.76,
      "end_seconds": 347.75,
      "duration_seconds": 16.99,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: This looks most like an underactive thyroid. I can't rule out anaemia yet. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've been feeling cold all the time, and no swelling in the neck or hair loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 348.62,
      "end_seconds": 350.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.95,
      "end_seconds": 354.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 355.33,
      "end_seconds": 356.16,
      "duration_seconds": 0.83,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.33,
      "end_seconds": 394.41,
      "duration_seconds": 26.08,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. I'd like to arrange a thyroid test for hypothyroid symptoms. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'm going to order blood tests, for fatigue. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'd like you to take levothyroxine, 50 micrograms, every morning on an empty stomach, until we review. You take it by mouth. That should help with hypothyroidism."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 395.85,
      "end_seconds": 398.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Alright, I'll pick it up today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 399.61,
      "end_seconds": 424.78,
      "duration_seconds": 25.17,
      "text": "Take the thyroid tablet on an empty stomach, half an hour before breakfast, and not with calcium or iron. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. Please don't sit on it if the symptoms get worse. That's the point to get seen urgently. I'd like to see you again after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 426.01,
      "end_seconds": 432.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 434.06,
      "end_seconds": 443.12,
      "duration_seconds": 9.06,
      "text": "So, I take the levothyroxine, 50 micrograms, every morning on an empty stomach and come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 444.23,
      "end_seconds": 449.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. We're all set. Don't leave without asking if something's unclear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 452.02,
      "end_seconds": 455.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "No, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 456.29,
      "end_seconds": 457.22,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}